From 2ac10e11df93d4ac3fecce6e49f1d0cdd0c9bcef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:54:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P4-printing-module-image-upload

Printing Module, Phase 4 (image upload vertical slice: storage + service + controller):

- LocalDiskPrintImageStorage (InfrastructureLayer/Storage - new folder, first component in
  this codebase that writes application content to the filesystem): extension allowlist ->
  magic-byte signature match (PNG/JPEG hardcoded; an operator-added AllowedExtensions entry
  with no matching signature fails closed, never silently trusts it) -> GUID physical name ->
  tenant-scoped write under a path resolved relative to ContentRootPath (not wwwroot).
  DeleteAsync is best-effort/never-throws per its IPrintImageStorage contract.
- PrintImageService: orchestrates storage + IUnitOfWork.PrintImages. Physical save happens
  OUTSIDE the DB transaction (mirrors BatchUploadService's decrypt/parse-outside-transaction
  structure - a physical write can never be rolled back by a DB transaction regardless of
  where it's called from). On a duplicate-name replace (Q-10), the old file's physical delete
  is deferred until AFTER the DB commit that removes its row succeeds - deleting it inline and
  then rolling back would leave the database pointing at a file that no longer exists, which
  is worse than the accepted orphan-file tradeoff.
- IServiceManager / ServiceManager: IPrintImageService wired through (12/12 property parity
  verified by script).
- InfrastructureServiceRegistration: PrintImageOptions, IPrintImageStorage, IPrintImageService
  + its Func<> registered.
- PrintImagesController: single POST /api/print-images endpoint, one-liner body, [FromForm]
  multipart binding matching InventoryController.Upload's precedent exactly.
- Program.cs: app.UseStaticFiles() scoped specifically to the resolved physical root (not a
  blanket wwwroot mount) via LocalDiskPrintImageStorage.ResolvePhysicalRoot, so the write path
  and serve path can never diverge. Flagged in-code: this serves images unauthenticated, by
  construction of static-file middleware (runs outside the MVC/[Authorize] pipeline) - GUID
  physical names, tenant-scoped paths, same posture as any link-shared asset, but not something
  the spec addressed explicitly.
- appsettings.json: PrintImages section added (validated as well-formed JSON).

Corrections to earlier phases, bundled in because they're one-line doc/default fixes directly
motivated by finishing this vertical slice:
- PrintImageOptions.RootPath default changed from wwwroot-relative to ContentRootPath-relative
  (P2 had assumed wwwroot before the static-file wiring was actually worked out)
- IPrintImageStorage.StoredImage.StoredPath and PrintImage.StoredPath doc comments corrected:
  tenant-relative (e.g. '7/<guid>.png'), not the full public imagePath - PrintImageService
  builds that by combining PublicBaseUrl + StoredPath

Bug caught during review before commit: extension allowlist check used Array.IndexOf against
a lowercased extension, which only matches if PrintImageOptions.AllowedExtensions entries in
configuration happen to already be lowercase. Fixed to a case-insensitive Array.Exists check.

Flagged for explicit confirmation:
- Static file serving is unauthenticated (see Program.cs comment above)
- The duplicate-name Warning text is hardcoded English, not localized - it isn't an Error, so
  it never passes through LocalizeErrorResultFilter (which only touches ApiError.Code); no
  existing mechanism localizes a success-path notice like this one
